      "why": [
        "\"Quant Developer (NLP)\" directly emphasizes probability theory, statistical analysis, and numerical modeling — core Jump research skills — plus a physics undergraduate background that aligns with their emphasis on physics/quantitative PhDs.",
        "Strong demonstrated research mindset: engineering adaptive circuit breakers with statistical thresholds, rigorous Pydantic validation pipelines reducing errors from 18% to 0.5%, and ML fundamentals (PyTorch, Transformers) relevant to Jump's modeling workflow.",
        "The resume explicitly frames work as hypothesis-driven testing and production validation against real data, mirroring Jump's philosophy of 'one excellent, fully understood result' and testing ideas against live systems."
      ],
